\fBNAME\fR
.br
.in 4n
usilic - pager and file manager
.in 0
.sp
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
.br
.in 4n
usilic [-c|-g] [-f font] [-s usec ...] [-d dot ...]
.br
         [file] [< file ...] [directory]
.in 0
.sp
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
.br
.in 4n
usilic works as a pager when started with standard input or regular files as arguments, and as a file manager when given a directory argument. After startup, the arguments can be checked on the first line ("OS name : command line") of the \fBINFO\fR screen shown by ^I (hold control and press "I"). The very first start opens in the \fBHELP\fR \fBmode\fR described below. From then on -H or ^T^H opens \fBHELP\fR, and -K or ^T^K opens \fBKEY\fR (all the key assignments), in another window, so try working while referring to the main functions and their usage.
.br
.sp
In a terminal that supports the mouse, scrolling by dragging the screen and with the wheel can be used. In addition, the left/right cursor keys start automatic scrolling, after which the up/down cursor keys adjust its speed.
.br
.sp
Note that in this manual page opened in \fBMAN\fR \fBmode\fR, moving to the previous / next chapter with the ; / : keys (defined in \fBMACRO\fR \fBmode\fR below) and following the notes shown underlined cannot be used.
.br
.sp
The main notations used in this text are as follows.
