.sp
.in 8n
The place ^X^X returns to (the mark) is put with ^␣, and also automatically on the line before ^[< / ^[>, a page scroll, the start of a search with ^S, a click on the scroll bar, or a move through a link; up to 16 marks are kept. ^X^X swaps the newest mark and the current line, and each ^U^␣ goes back through the marks from the newest. In lists with selection such as \fB(ls)\fR, ^␣ selects as before.
.in 0
.sp
.in 8n
The ^U count works with moving and repeating commands such as ^N/^P, j/k, page scrolls, n/p and ^Xe. ^Xz repeats the last command, including its ^U count. Registers (one character such as a) and bookmarks record a line of a file (the same line in a vertical book too) or a directory of \fB(ls)\fR. Registers last while usilic runs; bookmarks are kept in \*[usilic-i]~/.usilic/bookmarks\*[usilic-ie]. ^Xrm asks for a name (the file name by default); in the ^Xrb list, choose with ^N/^P and jump with ^M. ^M on a name prefixed with - deletes that bookmark.
.in 0
.sp
.in 19n
.ti 0n
File management  ：file manager\*[usilic-tab]
.in 0
.sp
.in 8n
